L310 -- THE INSTRUMENT SWEEP (all numbers committed):

   1. rotation curves (HI/CO/optical, outer halo)
      frame: 198/205/216 km/s at 30-100 kpc vs the 165 MOND-flat; d ln v/d ln r = +0.10..0.15 over 20-60 kpc (L305)
      LCDM:  flat-to-declining CDM halos
      discriminator: SIGN and SIZE of the outer slope
      recipe: Gaia-RVS + blue-HB halo stars at 20-100 kpc

   2. weak lensing, galaxy halo
      frame: outer slope steepening -2.0 -> -2.5; inner active cusp -1.71 MW class (L304/L309)
      LCDM:  -2.00 envelope / NFW -1.5 flat
      discriminator: the outer-halo lensing slope
      recipe: stacked weak-lensing profiles (DECaPS/CFHT), 30-100 kpc bins

   3. the RAR (stacked dynamics)
      frame: a0 = 9.3619e-11 with kappa = 1/2, NOT a fit (PD08); scatter = bias 1 by construction
      LCDM:  a0 fitted, scatter from halo variance
      discriminator: the intercept's curvature at g_N -> 0
      recipe: the SPARC + stacked samples at g_N < 0.1 a0

   4. strong lensing (Einstein radii)
      frame: interior active fraction ~0.5 x M_b at 5-20 kpc -> theta_E shrinks by ~0.8 (L304 profiles)
      LCDM:  NFW-halo theta_E (mass-concentration-sensitive)
      discriminator: the lens-ellipticity distortion
      recipe: SLACS/LENSCOLD lenses with resolved velocity profiles

   5. clusters: X-ray hydrostatic vs lensing
      frame: M_lens/M_X ~ 1.18 (L309: 4.9 vs 4.14x at delta_b = 70)
      LCDM:  M_X < M_lens (HSE bias) by ~10-20%
      discriminator: the bias MAGNITUDE at fixed gas T
      recipe: X-ray (Chandra/XMM) + stacked lensing on the same R500-interior

   6. clusters: SZ
      frame: the carrier's cold gas arrives at Mach 9.5 (L294): the kinetic-SZ of the infall adds to the thermal
      LCDM:  thermal-only SZ
      discriminator: the SZ signal outside the virialized core
      recipe: SZ imaging (SPT/ACT) with the infall-region masks

   7. clusters: caustic stacks (g04a)
      frame: -1.87 band slope; mass-dependent (MW -1.71, cluster -1.55 active faces) (L294/L298/L309)
      LCDM:  -1.5 at every mass (NFW)
      discriminator: the rise of cuspiness with mass
      recipe: caustic stacks vs weak-lensing halo mass

   8. CMB peaks
      frame: peak-window ratio 0.314 vs LCDM 0.315, FLAT across c_s^2 in {1e-11..1e-9} (L308b); the full face 0.991 vs 0.992 (L292)
      LCDM:  0.992 (measured)
      discriminator: the third-peak flatness of the carrier's sound window
      recipe: Planck TT

   9. CMB - recombination epoch
      frame: baryons-only face 1.192 vs 0.992: the third peak EXCLUDES the framework's baryons-only face at ~20-sigma (L295): the answer is the baryon-seeded dust (L307: R = 1.0000, alpha = 0)
      LCDM:  n/a
      discriminator: the peak budget
      recipe: Planck TT (committed falsifier)

  10. LSS P(k) / BAO
      frame: P/P_LCDM = 0.973/0.967/0.963 (z = 3), 0.987/0.983/0.974 (z = 0) (L292); BAO phase identical (adiabatic seeding)
      LCDM:  1.00
      discriminator: the BAO phase at fixed amplitude
      recipe: BOSS/DESI LRGs

  11. LSS growth / f-sigma8
      frame: sigma8 ratio 1.000000 with the sound-term error < 1e-4 at the LSS cells (L306/L308)
      LCDM:  1.00
      discriminator: the growth budget slope
      recipe: RSD (BOSS/DESI)

  12. LSS - the forest
      frame: c_s(z = 3) = 6.7 km/s <= 9.5 (L290): the carrier identical to CDM at the forest scales with the cold kinematic floor
      LCDM:  CDM (c_s = 0)
      discriminator: the small-scale cutoff
      recipe: Ly-alpha forest P(k), k = 5 h/Mpc

  13. dwarf satellites (L166)
      frame: c_s(alpha = 0.315) = 251 km/s: retained fraction 1.1e-4 <= 0.105 (L290-V6)
      LCDM:  CDM halos (retain everything)
      discriminator: the dwarf-mass dependence of retention
      recipe: the Classical dSphs' phase space (Gaia DR3 proper motions)

  14. galaxy dynamics vs lensing (the slip)
      frame: Psi = Phi to leading order, slip 4e-7; G_N = G/(1 - c14/2) (L279, Lean)
      LCDM:  1.000 GR
      discriminator: the slip at the 1e-6 level
      recipe: resolved stellar kinematics vs lensing in the same galaxies

  15. wide binaries
      frame: gamma_v = 1.000 (Amend 11)
      LCDM:  1.000 (GR)
      discriminator: gamma_v at the 1e-3 level
      recipe: Gaia wide-binary astrometry

  16. the binary-pulsar strong field
      frame: c_T = c, GW170817-consistent; PPN gamma = beta = 1 in the strong field (L280)
      LCDM:  1.000 GR
      discriminator: the dipole radiation absence
      recipe: double-neutron-star timing (PSR J0737)

  17. the solar system (PPN)
      frame: alpha_2 passes at c14 <= 8e-7 or the equal-speed locus c2 = c14/(1 - 2 c14) (L280, Lean); Cassini-consistent
      LCDM:  GR
      discriminator: alpha_2 at 1e-7
      recipe: LAGEOS/GP-B frame-dragging, Cassini

  18. the S8 tension
      frame: sigma8(carrier)/sigma8(LCDM) = 1.000000: the frame does NOT reproduce the S8 tension: it predicts the LCDM value (L306) -- a statement, not a cure
      LCDM:  the observed S8 ~ 0.76-0.83 (tension with Planck)
      discriminator: the growth budget
      recipe: all RSD+lensing combinations

SYNTHESIS: THE THREE-INSTRUMENT CLUSTER TEST: the frame predicts M_lens/M_X ~ 1.18 at fixed gas temperature (4.9 vs 4.14x, L309), the SZ to carry the infall's kinetic signature outside the virialized core (Mach 9.5, L294), and the caustic slope to rise with mass (-1.71 MW -> -1.55 cluster active faces). LCDM predicts M_X < M_lens (the HSE bias), thermal-only SZ, and a mass-FLAT -1.5 cusp.  Three instruments, three directional differences, one model.

